WEBVTT

00:04.410 --> 00:07.110
Raphael Hyurandell?

00:09.520 --> 00:11.570
What the hell is he doing here?!

00:28.170 --> 00:30.050
Let's have at it, then!

00:33.030 --> 00:34.510
Stop, Barbatos.

00:34.920 --> 00:38.080
Dammit! Did you eat my sorcery again?!

00:38.080 --> 00:41.020
Settle down. You're spoiling my drink.

00:41.020 --> 00:43.080
Why are you so relaxed?!

00:43.080 --> 00:44.730
You just gonna let this guy carve you up?!

00:45.020 --> 00:48.380
I don't think he's here to fight.

00:49.620 --> 00:51.660
<i>I don't sense any bloodlust or animosity.</i>

00:51.660 --> 00:53.030
<i>So what does he want?</i>

00:53.390 --> 00:56.150
Looks like there are some open 
seats. Care to join us?

00:57.320 --> 01:00.990
The new Archdemon seems to have 
a good head on his shoulders.

02:31.000 --> 02:36.010
<b>Episode 9:
The Angelic Knight Situation Sounds Like
 a Mess I'd Rather Not Get Involved In</b>

02:39.160 --> 02:41.340
<i>I invited him to sit down 
in the moment, but...</i>

02:41.650 --> 02:45.240
<i>I don't really have anything to 
say to this mountain of a man.</i>

02:45.240 --> 02:50.480
Mr. Sorcerer! My daughter... 
is my daughter gonna live?!

02:50.480 --> 02:54.610
How should I know?! Healing sorcery isn't 
really my thing, but I'll do what I can.

02:55.540 --> 02:57.680
I see why you're friends with Lord Zagan!

02:57.680 --> 02:59.290
I'm not his friend!

02:59.290 --> 03:01.280
<i>I'd rather be sitting over there.</i>

03:01.280 --> 03:04.660
<i>The girl's just unconscious.
 She doesn't even need any sorcery.</i>

03:06.830 --> 03:09.540
So, do you have some business with me...

03:09.800 --> 03:10.880
dragon slayer?

03:11.920 --> 03:16.430
The name is Raphael. I hear you've been
tangling with one my fellow knights.

03:16.430 --> 03:18.300
Which is why I wanted to get a look at you.

03:18.560 --> 03:20.260
<i>He must mean Chastille.</i>

03:20.760 --> 03:23.880
I must not look very remarkable,
 compared to you.

03:26.540 --> 03:30.390
And yet you look every bit the 
villain the rumors suggest.

03:30.720 --> 03:34.400
<i>That's rich coming from someone who 
can knock someone out with a grin.</i>

03:34.950 --> 03:38.120
I hear you've made a hobby 
out of killing sorcerers.

03:38.120 --> 03:42.200
And you don't mind two of them 
standing right in front of you?

03:43.250 --> 03:44.200
Don't be ridiculous.

03:45.430 --> 03:49.160
All I have ever done is snuff out 
embers that risk becoming an inferno.

03:49.500 --> 03:52.330
<i>That's not the story I've heard.</i>

03:52.330 --> 03:55.790
<i>Is this really a man who's 
killed nearly 500 sorcerers?</i>

03:56.130 --> 04:00.310
Archdemon, you've fought 
Chastille before, haven't you?

04:00.310 --> 04:03.550
Was she strong enough 
to pose a threat to you?

04:03.890 --> 04:05.520
I'm not sure.

04:05.520 --> 04:10.270
If nothing else, she was more formidable 
than anyone I've ever fought before.

04:11.420 --> 04:12.770
I see.

04:13.120 --> 04:17.360
That makes her a serious 
 threat to the Church.

04:18.760 --> 04:20.230
I don't get what you're saying.

04:20.550 --> 04:24.020
She objected against the 
hunt for Archdemon Zagan.

04:24.020 --> 04:27.740
That gives the Church more than 
enough reason to dispose of her.

04:28.960 --> 04:32.190
<i>That fool. Of all the awkward
positions to put herself in...</i>

04:32.190 --> 04:35.030
<i>She could've just pretended 
to go with the flow.</i>

04:35.990 --> 04:39.830
She never struck me as much 
of a survivor, but this?

04:39.830 --> 04:41.170
I'm with you on that point.

04:41.680 --> 04:45.760
Anyway, that concludes my business 
with you. I'll take my leave.

04:47.120 --> 04:49.140
<i>Wait, that's it.</i>

04:49.620 --> 04:52.770
<i>He came to confirm the link 
between Chastille and I.</i>

04:53.090 --> 04:56.100
<i>Looking for justification to strike her down.</i>

04:56.500 --> 04:57.320
Wait.

04:58.590 --> 05:01.730
That girl has her share 
of friends in this town.

05:02.080 --> 05:04.730
Plenty of whom would mourn her death.

05:05.470 --> 05:07.490
And this town happens to be my territory.

05:07.800 --> 05:10.870
If you step out of bounds, 
I'll make short work of you.

05:11.460 --> 05:14.040
That hardly sounds like something 
an Archdemon would say.

05:14.380 --> 05:16.920
Being an Archdemon affords 
me that kind of arrogance.

05:21.380 --> 05:24.840
You turned out to be just how I imagined!

05:25.190 --> 05:26.830
That sounds exactly like

05:26.830 --> 05:30.590
the kind of evil the Church would 
dedicate its resources to snuffing out.

05:33.600 --> 05:35.060
I don't like this.

05:35.400 --> 05:37.120
Did you really think you, a sorcerer,

05:37.120 --> 05:39.440
were gonna like what that guy, 
an Angelic Knight, had to say?

05:39.440 --> 05:42.840
Maybe you oughta chase the 
old timer down and kill him.

05:44.080 --> 05:46.280
Then get going, Barbatos.

05:47.760 --> 05:50.320
You telling me to die?! Is that it?!

05:50.320 --> 05:53.620
While I do want you to die, 
that's not what I meant.

05:54.100 --> 05:56.110
You want me to die?

05:56.110 --> 05:59.080
What I want you to do is check on Chastille.

06:00.850 --> 06:02.220
Why the hell would I?!

06:02.220 --> 06:07.190
It should be quick and easy with your 
teleportation sorcery, Barbatos the Purgatory.

06:07.190 --> 06:09.500
She's an Angelic Knight too, man.

06:09.500 --> 06:11.180
Are you serious about helping her?

06:11.490 --> 06:13.000
Just get going.

06:13.000 --> 06:16.140
I'll throw in some extra 
tomes to make it up to you.

06:17.690 --> 06:19.400
You're one weird bastard, y'know that?

06:22.140 --> 06:24.900
I'm pretty sure you're gonna regret this.

06:29.590 --> 06:31.240
Wait, he...

06:31.930 --> 06:34.540
<i>Left without paying the tab.</i>

06:35.020 --> 06:39.540
<i>I was the one who sent him away, 
but now I feel like he got one over on me.</i>

06:40.820 --> 06:43.110
Nephy should be asleep by now.

06:45.610 --> 06:47.800
Welcome home, Lord Zagan.

06:48.100 --> 06:49.080
Nephy?

06:49.880 --> 06:52.560
You could've gone to bed first.

06:52.560 --> 06:53.550
<b>Shhhh</b>

06:52.560 --> 06:53.800
Shhhh.

06:57.720 --> 07:02.150
For insisted on waiting until you got home.

07:03.070 --> 07:05.200
Yet she's already asleep.

07:05.200 --> 07:07.110
She worked very hard today.

07:07.510 --> 07:11.740
She helped carry all of the books we took 
from the Archdemon castle to the library.

07:12.830 --> 07:14.830
There were so many, too.

07:14.830 --> 07:18.500
Yes, but she wanted them to 
be ready for you to read.

07:18.880 --> 07:20.370
I see...

07:20.370 --> 07:22.040
For told me about it.

07:22.040 --> 07:26.210
How you said she could stay 
with you for a thousand years.

07:27.260 --> 07:30.670
I bet she was really happy to hear that.

07:33.610 --> 07:36.390
Dragons live extremely long lives.

07:36.390 --> 07:40.560
Anyone they can share that time 
with must seem really precious.

07:41.000 --> 07:45.430
Which also explains her vendetta against 
whoever killed her dragon parents.

07:47.020 --> 07:51.400
Maybe I should get rid of him 
before he encounters For.

07:51.780 --> 07:56.300
It would be nice if I could stay with 
you for that kind of time, too.

07:57.380 --> 07:58.700
What are you saying?

08:00.000 --> 08:02.210
You'll obviously be there, too.

08:03.350 --> 08:06.900
Right! I'll be with your side 
wherever you go, Lord Zagan!

08:12.400 --> 08:16.720
<i>Have Nephy's eyelashes always been this long?</i>

08:17.560 --> 08:20.640
<i>I feel like I haven't seen her 
up close like this before.</i>

08:20.640 --> 08:24.060
<i>To say nothing of how long it's been 
since we were alone together.</i>

08:25.910 --> 08:27.730
<i>She kinda smells nice.</i>

08:28.120 --> 08:29.900
<i>Did she just take a bath?</i>

08:29.900 --> 08:31.990
<i>Her hair's still a bit wet...</i>

08:32.440 --> 08:34.110
N-Nephy...

08:39.250 --> 08:40.700
Lord Zagan...

08:42.750 --> 08:44.540
Yo, Zagan, bad news!

08:46.890 --> 08:48.250
Come on, Zagan!

08:48.730 --> 08:51.510
Could you answer me?! You're the one who...

08:52.620 --> 08:56.640
Step outside, Barbatos. 
I'm gonna turn you into mincemeat.

08:56.990 --> 08:58.720
What are you so angry about?!

09:02.260 --> 09:03.350
Miss Chastille!

09:03.760 --> 09:04.980
It's poison.

09:05.390 --> 09:07.350
Seems like it was in her drink.

09:08.670 --> 09:10.270
Nephy, we'll treat her.

09:10.270 --> 09:11.600
I'll need your help.

09:11.600 --> 09:12.930
R-Right!

09:18.020 --> 09:19.870
You're too loud, Zagan.

09:20.130 --> 09:22.790
Sorry about that. You can go on to bed.

09:29.910 --> 09:31.040
An Angelic Knight!

09:38.320 --> 09:39.760
Whoa! Zagan!

09:44.010 --> 09:45.480
Why are you stopping me?

09:45.870 --> 09:49.060
She's my guest. You can't kill her.

09:51.530 --> 09:53.030
Do you hate the Angelic Knights?

09:53.580 --> 09:55.820
You must've figured it out, Zagan.

09:56.240 --> 09:59.910
I became a sorcerer to get 
revenge on the Angelic Knights!

10:00.390 --> 10:02.380
Is she the one who hurt you?

10:03.390 --> 10:06.410
Someone with a Sacred Sword killed my father!

10:06.770 --> 10:09.920
You're right, but it wasn't her, was it?

10:10.320 --> 10:14.700
You could kill her and the person you 
want revenge on wouldn't even care.

10:14.700 --> 10:17.380
All it would do is create 
more enemies for you.

10:17.860 --> 10:20.640
Enemies who would become additional 
obstacles for your revenge.

10:21.090 --> 10:23.010
It's a pretty common mistake, for greenhorns.

10:23.300 --> 10:25.220
What do you know, Zagan?!

10:28.560 --> 10:31.990
Revenge is about making your 
target suffer, endlessly,

10:31.990 --> 10:34.730
driving them into the depths 
of despair and terror...

10:35.250 --> 10:38.360
And making them beg for death.

10:40.790 --> 10:43.120
Then, if you're satisfied, you kill them,

10:43.120 --> 10:44.870
and that's when your revenge is complete.

10:45.360 --> 10:48.990
Simple revenge won't give you any solace.

10:48.990 --> 10:52.000
Did you ever get revenge before, Zagan?

10:52.470 --> 10:56.380
I did, but I failed. 
I killed him in an instant.

10:56.380 --> 11:00.260
<b>After all 
that 
torture
 I went 
through</b>

10:56.380 --> 11:00.260
<b>He died
in seconds...</b>

10:56.770 --> 11:00.260
And doing it didn't make me feel any better.

11:02.080 --> 11:07.290
Which is why, For, I'm going to teach 
you how to properly take your revenge.

11:08.140 --> 11:11.650
Fortunately for you, this castle has 
no shortage of torture implements.

11:16.880 --> 11:19.530
O-Okay...

11:20.870 --> 11:21.780
Man...

11:22.280 --> 11:25.990
You really wanna be teaching 
your kid that kinda thing?

11:25.990 --> 11:31.000
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

11:34.500 --> 11:35.460
Huh?

11:37.520 --> 11:38.630
Where am I?

11:38.910 --> 11:40.430
I see you're awake.

11:41.170 --> 11:42.660
Zagan?!

11:42.660 --> 11:44.660
You should thank Nephy.

11:44.660 --> 11:46.890
She's the one who treated you.

11:47.370 --> 11:48.680
Treated me?

11:48.680 --> 11:50.780
You were apparently poisoned.

11:51.390 --> 11:52.880
Anything come to mind?

11:52.880 --> 11:54.100
I'm not sure...

11:55.280 --> 11:58.730
Wait, I was summoned with a letter.

11:59.320 --> 12:01.600
There was no sender listed.

12:03.080 --> 12:07.370
The person I met was from the Church 
and mentioned a reconciliation faction.

12:07.760 --> 12:10.640
That they were in favor of 
coexistence and living together.

12:10.640 --> 12:14.010
The Church exists as a counter to sorcerers.

12:14.010 --> 12:16.790
We shouldn't go around killing them.

12:17.230 --> 12:19.670
We are a group who share this belief.

12:19.990 --> 12:23.180
I never knew such a faction existed.

12:23.720 --> 12:26.000
He never showed me his face.

12:26.000 --> 12:28.810
He said it'd be safer for 
both of us that way, for now.

12:29.920 --> 12:33.100
I felt like I recognized 
him from somewhere, but...

12:34.710 --> 12:36.940
Would you like to join us?

12:37.300 --> 12:41.940
Your defiance of the Church 
means you need protection.

12:43.350 --> 12:48.400
<i>If he's offering to help me... 
does he serve Cardinal Clavwell?</i>

12:48.400 --> 12:49.750
<i>No, but if that were the case...</i>

12:49.750 --> 12:51.750
I don't need an answer right away.

12:52.170 --> 12:53.960
But time is running short.

12:54.380 --> 13:00.960
For now... to prove I'm worthy of trust, 
should you need help, call out this name...

13:01.280 --> 13:02.460
"Orobas."

13:02.880 --> 13:04.550
That's what he said.

13:04.960 --> 13:06.680
Is that your name?

13:07.070 --> 13:10.360
You could say yes, and could say no.

13:10.360 --> 13:13.270
Think of it as the name of our leader.

13:13.520 --> 13:18.220
No matter what the situation, 
that name should protect you.

13:19.240 --> 13:21.910
<i>Can I really believe that?</i>

13:21.910 --> 13:24.340
<i>With Sir Raphael here,</i>

13:24.340 --> 13:28.530
<i>I probably shouldn't hesitate 
if I value my life.</i>

13:28.820 --> 13:32.000
<i>But... say I live, then what?</i>

13:32.000 --> 13:33.540
<i>What can I even do?</i>

13:34.230 --> 13:37.420
<i>All I know how to do is be an Angelic Knight.</i>

13:53.200 --> 13:55.100
There was poison in that tea?

13:55.370 --> 13:58.770
Any idea who could've poisoned you?

13:59.340 --> 14:03.440
I'm not sure. Sir Raphael would 
make the most sense, and yet...

14:03.940 --> 14:07.580
I doubt that. Not when he could've 
just lopped your head off.

14:03.940 --> 14:10.410
<b>Menacing...</b>

14:08.310 --> 14:10.410
You know about him?!

14:10.750 --> 14:11.880
I do indeed.

14:12.600 --> 14:15.910
In any case, you're apparently 
Nephy's friend...

14:16.330 --> 14:18.710
You can make yourself at home for now.

14:18.710 --> 14:19.790
W-Wait—

14:22.390 --> 14:23.670
What do you think you're doing?

14:26.400 --> 14:27.630
Well...

14:28.000 --> 14:32.140
Could you... stay for a bit longer?

14:32.960 --> 14:35.020
You should ask Nephy for that sort of thing.

14:36.800 --> 14:39.630
Yes. You're right.

14:39.630 --> 14:40.810
Forgive me.

14:48.640 --> 14:51.950
But it's not like we can 
wake her up at this hour.

14:51.950 --> 14:53.950
I'm just going to read.

14:55.090 --> 14:56.450
Thank you.

14:57.190 --> 15:00.040
<i>What was I trying to accomplish?</i>

15:00.660 --> 15:02.880
<i>Did I want him to turn my way?</i>

15:03.340 --> 15:07.840
<i>No. I want both Zagan and 
Nephy to find happiness.</i>

15:08.280 --> 15:09.300
<i>That's right.</i>

15:09.870 --> 15:14.850
<i>I think I want to be a part of the 
happiness they seem bound for.</i>

15:15.420 --> 15:19.100
<i>But in what way could that happen?</i>

15:24.580 --> 15:25.480
Well...

15:25.760 --> 15:29.050
How did I end up like this?!

15:29.050 --> 15:31.200
It suits you perfectly, Miss Chastille!

15:31.670 --> 15:35.220
I've never held a tool that 
wasn't a sword before.

15:35.220 --> 15:39.590
I said you could stay, but not for free.

15:39.590 --> 15:43.960
You're going to earn your keep while 
you're here. Just do what Nephy says.

15:44.400 --> 15:48.240
I understand, but could you 
be a bit more gentle about it?

15:48.240 --> 15:50.590
I'm feeling a bit pressured here.

15:52.480 --> 15:54.890
I saw you in town before.

15:55.240 --> 15:56.460
It's nice to meet you!

15:56.460 --> 15:59.100
Don't talk to me without cause, Tail-Head.

15:59.380 --> 16:01.270
T-Tail?

16:01.680 --> 16:04.180
What in the world did I do to her?

16:06.420 --> 16:10.360
Her father was apparently killed 
by a Sacred Sword wielder.

16:11.310 --> 16:15.970
You're not responsible for that, and I don't 
expect you to justify yourself to her.

16:15.970 --> 16:17.490
I just wanted you to understand.

16:17.810 --> 16:22.000
Wouldn't it be better if I left, then?

16:22.000 --> 16:25.000
No. You can leave For be.

16:25.000 --> 16:27.500
Young as she is, she's from a proud race.

16:27.880 --> 16:31.050
I doubt that pride would let 
her do anything foolish.

16:36.760 --> 16:37.800
Again?

16:38.260 --> 16:39.720
What is it this time?

16:40.240 --> 16:42.430
F-F-Frog!

16:42.750 --> 16:44.890
There's a frog!

16:45.290 --> 16:47.910
The third incident in so little time.

16:49.060 --> 16:50.460
Quit laughing!

16:50.460 --> 16:54.280
What happened to her pride keeping 
her from doing anything foolish?!

16:54.770 --> 16:59.160
Well, I'd say this is the result of her trying
 to harass you without resorting to her powers.

16:59.540 --> 17:01.180
She's still a child, after all.

17:01.180 --> 17:03.790
It's not strange that she'd 
express herself this way.

17:04.110 --> 17:07.010
You're pretty soft on her, aren't you?

17:07.010 --> 17:07.900
Am I?

17:15.860 --> 17:16.840
<i>This woman...</i>

17:17.220 --> 17:21.140
<i>She really is useless outside 
of a fight, it seems.</i>

17:21.140 --> 17:24.090
Well, you seem to be feeling 
a little better, at least.

17:30.030 --> 17:32.730
<i>Was he... worried about me?</i>

17:38.210 --> 17:40.620
<i>It's been ten days since the 
castle gained a new guest.</i>

17:41.060 --> 17:45.500
<i>Who would believe an Angelic Knight 
is living in an Archdemon's castle?</i>

17:45.840 --> 17:50.250
<i>But it's the truth. The woman is one of 
those wretched Sacred Sword wielders.</i>

17:50.640 --> 17:56.030
<i>Her name is apparently Chastille, but a 
fancy name like that is too much for her.</i>

17:56.030 --> 17:58.300
<i>Tail-Head works perfectly.</i>

17:58.300 --> 18:00.890
<i>And Tail-Head is a complete mess!</i>

18:06.400 --> 18:09.230
<i>She's supposed to be an Angelic Knight,
 but she couldn't dodge that?</i>

18:09.600 --> 18:13.150
<i>She's so pitiful, even I'm 
starting to feel sorry for her.</i>

18:23.360 --> 18:24.990
<i>I don't know how to put it...</i>

18:27.520 --> 18:30.010
<i>It's like messing with her is no challenge.</i>

18:34.150 --> 18:35.300
Have you got a moment?

18:37.430 --> 18:39.840
I'm sorry about how For's been acting.

18:39.840 --> 18:41.930
You don't need to apologize, Nephy.

18:44.350 --> 18:46.180
This is a lovely bath.

18:46.430 --> 18:51.230
Yes. Lord Zagan was nice enough to 
clean it up so that I could use it.

18:51.500 --> 18:52.810
I see...

18:53.780 --> 18:54.900
What is it?

18:54.900 --> 19:00.110
It's just, I realized how easily this 
place could accommodate both of you...

19:00.370 --> 19:04.760
Oh, that's right. We've been 
bathing together a lot lately.

19:05.520 --> 19:07.160
T-Together?!

19:07.160 --> 19:07.870
Yep.

19:08.240 --> 19:11.190
You probably wouldn't guess 
from how things are normally,

19:11.190 --> 19:13.710
but we can get pretty playful in the bath.

19:15.110 --> 19:17.460
P-Playful?!

19:17.920 --> 19:20.710
Washing each other's hair, 
and then clinging to each other...

19:20.710 --> 19:22.970
C-Clinging?!

19:23.440 --> 19:25.450
She's a sweet girl deep down.

19:25.450 --> 19:28.220
I'm sure the two of you will 
become friends someday.

19:31.180 --> 19:33.960
Uh, let's clear something up.

19:33.960 --> 19:36.520
When you talk about bathing together...

19:37.490 --> 19:38.740
I meant For.

19:39.170 --> 19:41.660
Of course! You meant For! Obviously!

19:42.650 --> 19:45.160
What could I have been thinking?

19:45.760 --> 19:47.620
Who else could you have...

19:47.620 --> 19:49.470
No, w-we couldn't!

19:53.120 --> 19:56.750
Are you here to lecture me 
about what I did to Tail-Head?

19:57.120 --> 20:00.000
If you understand that, 
then show some restraint.

20:00.000 --> 20:01.480
What kind of restraint?

20:01.480 --> 20:03.590
Well, let's see...

20:03.590 --> 20:06.640
No pranks during meals or involving food.

20:07.000 --> 20:08.860
I know that much.

20:08.860 --> 20:11.770
And I remember you said not to kill her.

20:12.640 --> 20:14.350
I guess anything else is fine, then.

20:15.760 --> 20:17.230
It is?

20:17.710 --> 20:20.860
Listen, For, Nephy and
 I have talked it over...

20:21.290 --> 20:24.070
Do you want to keep living here?

20:25.770 --> 20:28.780
We were already assuming that you would,

20:28.780 --> 20:31.630
but I thought I should check how you feel.

20:32.150 --> 20:34.210
But... I...

20:34.650 --> 20:38.320
If you've got something that needs doing, 
you can answer after it's taken care of.

20:38.320 --> 20:40.130
You're free to do as you like.

20:40.500 --> 20:42.660
Just remember this:

20:43.160 --> 20:45.390
Nephy and I will always be waiting.

20:47.440 --> 20:48.890
Thank you.

20:56.880 --> 20:58.020
Father...

20:59.120 --> 21:00.570
Father, where are you?

21:38.730 --> 21:40.980
<b>Squeeze</b>

21:38.730 --> 21:40.980
Frogs...

21:39.230 --> 21:40.980
<b>Squeeze</b>

21:39.730 --> 21:40.980
<b>Uuugh....</b>

21:42.160 --> 21:45.900
It would be easier if she 
would draw her sword in anger.

21:47.780 --> 21:49.520
Lord Zagan!

21:50.920 --> 21:52.490
What is it, Nephy?

21:52.980 --> 21:53.880
For...

21:54.880 --> 21:56.000
For is...

21:56.460 --> 21:58.240
For is gone!

23:30.010 --> 23:35.010
<b>Next Time: 
Of Course Parents Panic When Their
 Daughter Runs Away From Home</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:39.980
<b>Ugh...
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hUgh....</b>
